  "title": " Want to Limit Risk? Start with This One Contract Clause.",
  "date": "2025-05-27T14:32:12.586Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n A tale of timelines, lawsuits, and bundles of sticks.\n\n Want to Limit Risk? Start with This One Contract Clause.\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about timelines. Specifically, how long your reps and warranties should stick around after your business deal closes.\nIf you\u2019re selling, you probably don\u2019t want a buyer showing up three years later saying, \u201cSurprise! You owe me money for that thing I just discovered.\u201d\nIf you\u2019re buying, you absolutely want that runway\u2014because you won\u2019t know everything about the business until you\u2019ve lived through a full annual cycle (or two).\nEnter: the survival clause.\nThis clause limits how long certain representations and warranties survive after closing. In other words, it\u2019s a contractual expiration date on how long you can be sued for stuff you promised.\nSellers want shorter. Buyers want longer. Welcome to the eternal tug-of-war that is deal negotiation.\nWhat\u2019s typical? I\u2019ve seen 12 months, 18 months, 24, even 36. Personally, I like 18 months for buyers\u2014it gives you a year to uncover issues, plus a little breathing room to hire a lawyer and actually do something about it.\nSellers? You\u2019re gunning for 12. Anything longer gives the buyer time to discover problems and get their legal ducks in a row.\nAlso\u2014let\u2019s not forget about the statute of limitations. Just because the contract doesn\u2019t say how long reps survive doesn\u2019t mean there\u2019s no limit. But it does mean that limit could be a looooong time.\nAnd unless you\u2019re trying to fund your lawyer\u2019s next vacation home, I recommend putting something in writing.\nTo smarter timelines and fewer lawsuits,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
